Z||000000||Gokart||06-19-2000||09:28 PM||||Could someone tell me what degree thermostat I should be using with the warmer weather coming. I forgot. I had the right one in for the winter and misplaced the summer one I had last year. TKS  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Gokart (edited 06-19-2000).]||||reg||5
Z||000001||deceler8||06-19-2000||09:29 PM||||I use 180 summer, 195 winter.||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||06-20-2000||12:35 AM||||I use the stock 195 year round, and my temp meter reads about 5-10 degrees higher in summer (180 by the factory meter).  Rock steady, as long as I'm not sitting in traffic, and the fan kicks on right below the red mark if I am stopped for a while.  In that case, if I turn the AC on (mine's removed), the temp shoots right back down to normal.  I live in SE Georgia, 90 degrees + most of the summer, but this has been the exact same for the last 12 years, and I've lived in VA, MN, WA, and CT during that time.  ||||reg||1
